<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aurès Mountains</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aurès</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Aurès Mountains are a range of the Saharan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlas-mountains">Atlas</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, home of the Chaoui <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berbers</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> the legion at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lambaesis">Lambaesis</a> guarded their northern edge, and after the Vandal conquest Berber kingdoms held them. They were a base of resistance to the Arab conquest under the Kahina and, in 1954, the starting point of Algeria's war of independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aures-mountains.jpg" alt="Aurès Mountains" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ghezal Tarek · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hammam_Essalhine_Aquae_Flaviane_Khenchela_Mont_View_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
